 "discoveries": [
  "DISCOVERY: (claim) Folding the four raw l_nv bits into site 0 (3 CX/side) replaces site 0's transcoder AND: three cleaning ANDs (sites 1-3) already make the bright move X on f_0 and give the class bit p for free; qiskit rccx fails here (its +-i phases give +-i partner ratios when w_0=1), a real-phase Margolus Toffoli (3 CX, 4 T) is exact.",
  "DISCOVERY: (claim) In this frame no dark flag is needed: a Walsh multiplexer with 17-18 terms, all coefficients +-beta/8 or +-beta/4, is exact on all 433 states (HiGHS, time-limited; LP bound 16 terms without outer bits), but its parities are heavy and cost 30 CX after routing (beam-searched CX network), so the frame's AND saving is eaten by the multiplexer.",
  "DISCOVERY: (claim) Adding one NOR flag of two dark bits (6 CX) shortens the routed multiplexer only to 28 CX; outer l_2v(0) = d_0 on w_0=0 is a free mux control but saves just 1 term."
 ],
 "summary": "native 3-AND frame (raw l_nv parity folded into site 0, Margolus Toffolis on sites 1-3, f-collapse) puts the bright move on f_0; an ungated 17-term Walsh multiplexer (30 CX) over invariant data bits and one outer bit replaces the bright flag; 76 CX, valid but above the 71-CX archive best.",
